From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:43:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] open the Bukkit scoreboard API under region rules

Folia blocks five scoreboard methods with an unconditional throw; the
implementations behind them are intact. Open them under region-architecture
rules instead of single-main-thread rules:

- plugin boards: creation and structural changes broadcast through netty and
  a copy-on-write player list, both thread-safe, so any tick thread may do
  them (the async catcher still rejects true async creation)
- the main board is persisted global state: structural changes require the
  global tick thread - the same thread the vanilla /scoreboard command uses -
  and fail loudly with attribution anywhere else
- assigning a board to a player is per-player display state: owning region
  only, verified (never inferred), loud failure otherwise

The manager's board collection becomes a concurrent weak set because every
region's stat/death hot path iterates it (forAllObjectives) while boards are
created on other tick threads; the old WeakCollection is a bare ArrayList
whose iterator also prunes cleared refs, so even reads mutate it. No lock on
the hot path. The player's board override becomes volatile for the same
cross-thread readers.

